</div>',
  '<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Client Profiles to Target</div>
<p><strong>DIY investors who saw Friday''s headline and sold or are considering selling:</strong> The 803-point TSX decline is alarming without context. A self-directed investor who does not have the sector attribution or the year-to-date frame has no basis for the decision they are about to make.</p>
<p><strong>Investors overweight technology or U.S. growth who had no Canadian energy exposure:</strong> This population underperformed the TSX in both directions: they missed the Hormuz energy trade on the way up and participated fully in the Nasdaq-linked decline on Friday. The conversation is about portfolio construction, not just Monday''s market.</p>
<p><strong>Near-retirement investors who experienced Thursday''s high and Friday''s reversal as a warning sign:</strong> The sequence reads as a peak-and-reversal pattern to investors without a longer frame. This is the classic availability-heuristic prospect that the Behavioural Desk covered this morning.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Opening Line</div>
<div class="script-box">I am calling because the TSX hit an all-time high Thursday and fell 2.3% Friday, and I want to make sure you have the full picture before making any decisions based on that sequence.</div>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Value Proposition</div>
<p>The difference between Thursday''s 35,217 and Friday''s 34,413 is 803 points. The difference between understanding why is the difference between a client who holds through the recovery and one who crystallizes a loss at the worst moment. The year-to-date gain, the sector attribution of Friday''s decline, the BoC calendar, and the oil price context are all pieces of information that a self-directed investor checking a portfolio app on a Saturday morning does not have access to in assembled form. An advisor assembles them in three minutes.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Discovery Questions</div>
<p>Did you check your portfolio after Friday''s close, and what was your initial reaction to what you saw?</p>
<p>How is your portfolio currently split between Canadian equities, U.S. equities, and fixed income?</p>
<p>Do you have meaningful exposure to the energy sector, and have you thought about what happens to those positions if a Hormuz deal is announced?</p>
<p>With the Bank of Canada deciding Wednesday, do you have any mortgage or fixed income holdings that you are watching in relation to the rate decision?</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
