Friday''s decline was driven by a U.S. jobs report that came in at more than double the expected number. That pushed U.S. bond yields higher and triggered a tech-led selloff in North American markets. The Nasdaq fell nearly 5%. The TSX fell considerably less because Canadian energy names held relatively well with oil near $90.<br><br>
The TSX is still up more than 10% for the year. This was a meaningful single-session decline from a record high, not a structural break. But understanding the difference matters for whether you hold or sell on Monday morning.<br><br>
If you are trying to make sense of your portfolio in this environment and doing it alone, I would be glad to talk through the picture with you. No commitment required.<br><br>
